d other weird stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T12:15:12-07:00","id":1505575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1505296-trinity-player-s-guide-backerkit-crowdfunding?p=1505542#post1505542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the book on Talents, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a combination of the Talents Player's Guide and the book on strange places, other dimensions, etc. which were formerly separate but now have been integrated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-17T14:12:37-07:00","id":1505589,"title":"","content":"... With Talents getting powers to GET TO those Strange Places and Dimensions. \ud83d\ude0e","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-20T20:31:57-07:00","id":1506007,"title":"","content":"Qoueting on Ian from official forum topic...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1506003-crowdfunding-trinity-continuum-player-s-guide#post1506003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The <b>Trinity Continuum Player's Guide</b> will be launching on <i>Crowdfunding by BackerKit</i> on Tuesday, March 28th at 2pm EDT. ( Edit by me - Also, this Friday we have whole Pathcast episode on TPG! \ud83d\ude0e)<ul><li>This project combines the previously in-development <b>Talent Player's Guide</b> and <b>Brave New Worlds</b> into a single book!</li> <li>Full writeups for the &quot;Lesser&quot; Allegiances from the TC core: Alert Status 1, Les Fant\u00f4mes, the National Office of Emergency Research, La R\u00e9volte \u00c9clatante, The Theseus Club, the Transcendent Alliance, and now including Polyphemus!</li> <li>Guidelines for travelling through time, through planetary gates to other worlds, to other dimensions, into the microverse, and undersea!</li> <li>Tons of new Gifts and systems to boost your Talents!</li> </ul><img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/optimized_TCPG_Video_Splash.png\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/optimized_TCPG_Video_Splash.png\" data-thumb-url=\"http://theonyxpath.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/03/optimized_TCPG_Video_Splash.png\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T11:35:08-07:00","id":1506328,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><a href=\"https://onyxpathcast.podbean.com/e/episode-252-a-guide-for-talented-trinity-players/\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Pathcast about <i>Trinity Player\u2019s Guide</i> coming on crowdfunding in this Tuesday.</b></a> <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude0e</span></span><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">12:30 - <b>In book there are Alternative Dimensions/Realities</b> \u2013 and Dimension hoping. There are like<b> Gates</b>, but do not need to be <b>Stargate</b>-like runic big rings. For example, they can work as specific doors. Sometimes you can stumble through.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">15:00 - <b>Talents ARE supernatural, but can THINK they are not.</b> Talents can interact with those portals, normal people would normally not \u2013 but baselines can slip through them, from time to time.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">16:00 \u2013 <b>Gates/Portals</b> can also can works to future settings, past settings and other worlds, even alien planets from Aeon! <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude2e</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">21:00 \u2013 <b>Gates</b> MAYBE are related to <b>Aether</b> Gates \u2013 but modern Talents do not need to have some device to open them. <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude2e</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">22:30 \u2013 <b>\u2018Chapter on Doing Things\u2019</b> <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude09</span> \u2013 Expanding subsystems, like Chase Scenes ( \u2018Fast &amp; Furious\u2019 style ), cool Environments, how Talents can change Environment on WILL <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude2e</span>, Dogfights from planes. How to do Heists \u2013 Heist system to run like \u2018Oceans Eleven\u2019 \u2013 Dramatic Editing for \u2018heisting\u2019.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">34:30 \u2013 <b>\u2018Chapter on Goodies\u2019</b> \u2013 New Gifts, some from previous books \u2013 each one is pointed to from which books came from. Assassins Masteries are re-written as Gifts for (modern day) Talents. NEW Gifts are about dimension travels, Gates, even going for Microverse. And just new Gifts, totally for TC Core. Gifts having different versions based on your higher Facets. And how to write new Gifts, on general. New Edges \u2013 for different settings, heisting, chasings. New Paths.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">45:00 \u2013 <b>There are Super Science items!</b> Gear items, vehicles. For example, <b><i>Telluric Intruder</i></b> car. Strange vehicle looks a lot like DeLorean with <b><i>Flux Capacitor</i></b> tag \u2013 that makes you 1 point lower using Dramatic Editing for scene. <span style=\"font-family:Segoe UI Emoji\">\ud83d\ude2e</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">49:00 \u2013 <b>Minor Allegiances</b> write-ups &amp; <b>Flux Stunts</b>.</span></li> <li><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">54:00 \u2013 No <b>\u2018Next Level of Talents\u2019</b>, like Max Mercer or Nicola Tesla \u2013 no Next Levels in Modern times, but they are Magogs in <b>Aether </b>as those Advanced Talents</span>\u200b</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-25-2023, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T11:45:01-07:00","id":1506329,"title":"","content":"Okay; <i>this</i> is the book I've been looking for ever since <b>Trinity Continuum</b> was first announced.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T12:41:18-07:00","id":1506336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1505296-trinity-player-s-guide-backerkit-crowdfunding?p=1506328#post1506328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">54:00 \u2013 No <b>\u2018Next Level of Talents\u2019</b>, like Max Mercer or Nicola Tesla \u2013 no Next Levels in Modern times, but they are Magogs in <b>Aether </b>as those Advanced Talents</span>\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify: Mercer isn't covered because it'd be too damn difficult to translate what he does mechanically (though there is considerable coverage of past time travel), Tesla <i>is</i> via the Gates and all the stuff that comes with them.<br /> <br /> Magogs are a useful model for high-level Talents, absent the Magog Deviations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T14:31:19-07:00","id":1506364,"title":"","content":"My only concern is whether high-level Talents will still feel like, well, talents. High-level Gifts can certainly be beyond regular human capacity, even overtly so; but for the most part, I would expect them to be rooted in competence: things like ninja invisibility (your ability to sneak around gets upgraded to impossible levels), wuxia wire-working (applying athletics to the point where you're running up walls or drifting through the air in defiance of the laws of gravity), or more modern gun-fu offerings (most famously involving bullets that don't follow straight-line trajectories). The sort of things that one might expect of contemporary equivalents of <b>Exalted</b>'s protagonists. <br /> <br /> The line between that and Novas is a fuzzy one; for instance, the earliest concept of Wonder Woman would have fit firmly in the \u201chigh-level Talent\u201d concept as I imagine it, despite her capabilities being more or less the same then as they are now. But I feel that it's important that there at least be a significant portion of the high-level Gifts that are Skill-based.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T17:58:15-07:00","id":1506388,"title":"","content":"I just listened to the Podcast. Some clarifications and thoughts: <br /> <br /> First, nobody involved in the creation of the book said that high-level Talents would bear any resemblance to <b>\u00c6ther</b>'s Magogs; <i>that</i> comment was made by the host. And personally, I think he got it wrong: Magogs are based on \u00c6ther, which is <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">a blend of Flux and Quantum, and owes as much to <b>Aberrant</b> as it does to Talents.</div></div> </div> </div> That was the main point of my last post. <br /> <br /> Next, I misread something in wyrdhamster's last post; so in case anyone else did the same, let me point out that TPG will <i>not</i>, repeat <b><i>not</i></b>, be including high-level Talents. Which is fine by me; because what I'm looking for is actually a tier of \u201cTalents\u201d that's higher than regular Talents (in that they can do blatantly impossible things), but still below the level of Max Mercer; and it's the \u201cMax Mercer\u201d level that the podcast's guests described when they said that they're never going to write rules for high-level Talents.<br /> <br /> Psychics have mesmerists and psiads at a base level, psions at an intermediate level, and proxies as the top-tier Psi-empowered; Quantum-powered heroes range from stalwarts, Superiors, and Dark Stars as the \u201chard to distinguish from baselines\u201d bottom tier, Novas as the middle tier, and Transcended Novas as the top tier. I view Talents as the bottom tier of the Flux-wielders, and Max Mercer as the top tier; and I have no interest in games that operate at that upper level; so the reveal that they intend to never touch that level is perfectly okay with me.<br /> <br /> But conceptually, there's a \u201cmiddle tier\u201d here as well, where the characters are able to do blatantly impossible things, but aren't so OP that they need to mostly remain in Storyguide hands else they'll break the game. The \u201cmiddle tier\u201d is more like <b>Assassins</b>, but without its near-monomaniacal focus on one type of story (i.e., everything's geared around the way assassin movies play): my \u201chigh-tier Talents\u201d would wield Masteries, but with none of this business about everything necessarily being divided between Preparation, Evaluation, and Execution. <br /> <br /> Which brings me to Heists. What I'm hearing about them makes me think that they cover much of the same ground as <b>Assassins</b> does with its Hunt mechanics, but with less of a straitjacket feel to it \u2014 largely because it's <i>fully optional. </i>The Masteries in <b>Assassins</b> assume that you'll be playing within the story structure of a Hunt, to the extent that <i>which phase of the Hunt that you're in</i> is built into their write-ups. As far as I can tell, there will be a few Gifts and Edges designed with Heists in mind; but for the most part, Gifts and Edges will be more broadly applicable than that. <br /> <br /> As well, not every Mastery from <b>Assassins</b> will be ported into <b>Trinity Player's Guide</b> as a Gift; only the ones that it would make sense for regular Talents to have as Gifts will be converted, along with daredevil and Squire Gifts from <b>Adventure!</b> and <b>\u00c6ther</b> that likewise would make sense for a modern-day Talent to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-24T21:47:21-07:00","id":1506402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1505296-trinity-player-s-guide-backerkit-crowdfunding?p=1506364#post1506364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only concern is whether high-level Talents will still feel like, well, talents.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's why I wrote and run <i>starting </i>Max Mercer in 1923 as sorta Adept Time Mage ( 4 th dot powers ) from<b> Mage the Awakening</b> for my <b>Adventure!</b> story - it was easier to grasp mechanically him. \ud83d\ude0e It played good enough, in my POV.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1505296-trinity-player-s-guide-backerkit-crowdfunding?p=1506364#post1506364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">High-level Gifts can certainly be beyond regular human capacity, even overtly so; but for the most part, I would expect them to be rooted in competence: things like ninja invisibility (your ability to sneak around gets upgraded to impossible levels), wuxia wire-working (applying athletics to the point where you're running up walls or drifting through the air in defiance of the laws of gravity), or more modern gun-fu offerings (most famously involving bullets that don't follow straight-line trajectories). The sort of things that one might expect of contemporary equivalents of <b>Exalted</b>'s protagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, simply, <b>John Wick</b>'s levels of mayhem. \ud83d\ude1c Funny you wrote that - literally 3 days ago I made antagonists NPC for our <b>Assassins</b> game. He is Swarm/Yakuz (both) ninja-like captain. I introduce him that he shows up in players apartament balcony, silent as night, without any sound, with cherry petals on the wind only marking his existence... Thanks for more ideas on his powers.\ud83d\ude08<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1505296-trinity-player-s-guide-backerkit-crowdfunding?p=1506364#post1506364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The line between that and Novas is a fuzzy one; for instance, the earliest concept of Wonder Woman would have fit firmly in the \u201chigh-level Talent\u201d concept as I imagine it, despite her capabilities being more or less the same then as they are now. But I feel that it's important that there at least be a significant portion of the high-level Gifts that are Skill-based.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, classical ear <b>Wonder Women</b> - when she was really WONDER in comics - would nicely gel with High(or maybe Medium?)-Level Talents.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-26T14:52:30-07:00","id":1506535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1505296-trinity-player-s-guide-backerkit-crowdfunding?p=1506388#post1506388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just listened to the Podcast. Some clarifications and thoughts:<br /> <br /> First, nobody involved in the creation of the book said that high-level Talents would bear any resemblance to <b>\u00c6ther</b>'s Magogs; <i>that</i> comment was made by the host. And personally, I think he got it wrong: Magogs are based on \u00c6ther, which is <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">a blend of Flux and Quantum, and owes as much to <b>Aberrant</b> as it does to Talents.</div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>Um, no it isn't. Quantum and \u00c6ther are only 'related'; in two ways:<br /> 1).<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The Quantum powered industrial sized dimensional travel machines used by the 'Martians' produces \u00c6ther as a side effect by essentially squeezing Flux through a sausage grinder. The Quantum and Flux aren't mixing.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> 2).<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">The 'Martians' and their machines are so contaminated by \u00c6ther (due to traveling via their industrial sized dimensional transfer machines) that every single time they activate a Quantum power, a bit of \u00c6ther is burned off, generating a green glow. Again, the two energies aren't mixing.</div></div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T14:40:00-07:00","id":1506791,"title":"","content":"BackerKit crowdfunding started - and we are already almost at goal of 15k$! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.backerkit.com/c/onyx-path/trinity-continuum-player-s-guide\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.backerkit.com/c/onyx-pat...player-s-guide</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-29-2023, 10:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-29T07:52:07-07:00","id":1506849,"title":"","content":"As to the first preview - we got <b>Intro and Allegiances </b>in this package.<br /> <br /> For now, <b>Alert Status 1</b> looks nice <b>Mission Impossible</b> -like organization.<br /> <br /> <b>La R\u00e9volte \u00c9clatante</b> let's join rebels and be, for example, Black Lives Matters protests ex-organiser, now real life terro... freedom fighter.\u200b<br /> <br /> <b>Les Fant\u00f4mes</b> are <b>Carmen Sandiego</b> and <b><a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt2531336/\" target=\"_blank\">Lupin</a></b> alike 'good thieves'.<br /> <br /> <b>NOER</b> are nice take on <b>X-Files</b> and <b>Fringe</b> government agencies looking over Flux incidents - with added more open rooster to other associates Talents types in it?<br /> <br /> <b>Polyphemus</b> are private ( based on Aeon Society project ) counterpart to NOER - based on <b>Control</b> game concepts and with <b>Loki</b> TV series <b>TVA</b> agency aesthetics ( 60s bureaucratic surrealism )?<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> 